    "head": "scenario/ex20-nest-bootstrap"
  },
  "explains": "A line is added to bootstrap in src/main.ts (app.enableCors()). The file creates the application and sets the global prefix; whatever it registers (pipes, guards, filters, the prefix) applies to every controller, so every route of the service is reached: the four of LedgerController and the two of BalancesController. BalancesController is decorated with a version, which Nest puts in the path, and src/main.ts enables URI versioning (app.enableVersioning with VersioningType.URI): the path is kept with the unknown part marked, flagged partial, and the run says so (route_path_partial, at the controller decorator). The console calls BALANCES_URL, /api/ledger/balances, which fits the partial balances route only through its unknown segment: that is a match by name, so BalancesScreen (/balances) is a candidate, shown apart and never must-test. The audit and reports controllers are served by nothing, so the bootstrap reaches none of their routes and nothing is said about them.",
